Market Challenges
Verification providers must assess complex industrial processes, emissions calculations, precursor materials and energy records across international supply chains. Differences in documentation quality, local regulations and technical capabilities can make consistent verification difficult.

Market Restraints
The availability of default emissions values may reduce the incentive for some importers to commission independent verification. Exemptions for smaller importers, limited accreditation capacity and the cost of on-site assessments may also restrict the addressable market.

