Emerging Market Opportunities
The expansion of carbon border reporting frameworks is creating opportunities for accredited verification, independent emissions data assurance and pre-verification services. Providers with international audit networks and industry-specific expertise may benefit from demand across steel, aluminium, cement, fertiliser, hydrogen and electricity supply chains.

Regional Market Insights
Asia-Pacific accounted for an estimated 43% of the market in 2025, supported by its manufacturing and export base and the need for emissions documentation among suppliers serving international markets.

Europe remains important as a regulatory centre for carbon border adjustment implementation. North America, Latin America and the Middle East and Africa also present opportunities as exporters and industrial producers respond to evolving carbon reporting requirements.

